---
layout: page
---
{%- comment -%}
  LOCAL OVERRIDE of al_folio_core's _layouts/profiles.liquid.

  Renders staff as a three-column grid matching the sibling course site
  https://ntu-ev.github.io/instructors/ instead of the gem's default
  one-per-row list. Three changes from the gem's copy:
    - `.profile` -> `.profile-three-col` (grid cell; styles in _sass/_rpl.scss)
    - the per-profile `<hr>` separator is dropped
    - the per-profile content block becomes a single trailing clearfix, so the
      floated cells do not overlap the footer

  `page.content` is intentionally not rendered per profile: the gem repeated it
  under every entry. Styles live in _sass/_rpl.scss.

  After bumping al_folio_core, re-diff with:
    bundle exec al-folio upgrade overrides diff _layouts/profiles.liquid
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="post">
  <article>
    {% if page.profiles %}
      {% for profile in page.profiles %}
        <div class="profile-three-col float-{% if profile.align == 'left' %}left{% else %}right{% endif %}">
          {% if profile.image %}
            {% assign profile_image_path = profile.image | prepend: 'assets/img/' %}
            {% if profile.image_circular %}
              {% assign profile_image_class = 'img-fluid z-depth-1 rounded-circle' %}
            {% else %}
              {% assign profile_image_class = 'img-fluid z-depth-1 rounded' %}
            {% endif %}
            {% capture sizes %}(min-width: {{ site.max_width }}) {{ site.max_width | minus: 30 | times: 0.3}}px, (min-width: 576px) 30vw, 95vw"{% endcapture %}
            {% include figure.liquid loading="eager" path=profile_image_path class=profile_image_class sizes=sizes alt=profile.image %}
          {% endif %}
          {% if profile.more_info %}
            <div class="more-info">{{ profile.more_info }}</div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

      {% endfor %}
      <div class="clearfix"></div>
    {% endif %}
  </article>
</div>
